  "gaps": [
    "Catalog year/term is not stated on the page.",
    "The page states 'credit hours' but does not explicitly say semester hours; semester system is assumed.",
    "Program title is printed in two forms ('online associate's degree of multidisciplinary studies' and 'The Associate Degree in Multidisciplinary Studies').",
    "Inconsistency: the requirements text lists a 9-credit Framework (STS 110, MA 100, EN 100) that all students must complete, while the summary graphic labels 9 credits as 'Elective Credits'. Whether Framework courses can be waived or replaced by electives (e.g., via placement or transfer) is not stated.",
    "Written Communication is labeled 9 credit hours and the Foundational block 15 credit hours; the listed blocks sum correctly, but no substitution rules are given.",
    "CIS 111, CIS 115, CIS 121, and CIS 212 appear in both the general-education Technology category and the major lists, and the Additional Requirements list repeats the first two major lists. The capture does not state whether one course may satisfy more than one requirement.",
    "No residency (courses that must be completed at Bellevue) requirement is stated.",
    "Minimum grade, GPA, and transfer-credit limits are not stated. The page directs readers to consult an admissions counselor and the BRUIN 'Academic Progress' tool.",
    "The capture includes a 'show me more' control, so additional curriculum content may not have been captured."
  ],
